  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nWednesday will be a transition day as the Pacific low gradually\nexits the region. Some morning scattered showers are likely to\nstill be across the far eastern Arizona high terrain, but any \nactivity should quickly wind down in the afternoon. Elsewhere on \nWednesday, sunny skies and warmer temperatures are forecast for \nsoutheast California and southwest Arizona while the south- \ncentral Arizona lower deserts will see some lingering clouds and \nwell below normal temperatures.\n\nModel guidance shows upper level ridging fully moving into our\nregion on Thursday and likely staying put through the upcoming\nweekend. This will lead to gradual drying and mostly clear skies\nwhile temperatures slowly rise closer to the normal range for the\nsouth-central Arizona lower deserts. The western lower deserts \nmay reach 100 degrees again starting Friday, but for the eastern \nhalf of Arizona some reinforcing cooler air from the east Friday \nthrough Saturday should keep daytime highs at or just above 90 \ndegrees through Saturday. This cooler easterly flow may even \ncontinue into early next week with temperatures in the Phoenix \narea staying right near seasonal normals for early October.",
